COMMERCIAL CI/CD LICENSE REQUIRED
==================================

If you are a for-profit company or organization and you run covtest in
server-side automated build, test, or continuous integration / continuous
delivery (CI/CD) pipelines, you must obtain a commercial license by sponsoring
the project.

Sponsorship tiers and pricing: https://github.com/sponsors/memsharded

"Server-side" means any execution that is not on an individual developer's own
workstation — including but not limited to cloud CI services (GitHub Actions,
GitLab CI, Jenkins, CircleCI, Azure Pipelines, etc.), on-premise build servers,
and automated test runners that are not triggered interactively by a developer.


